p.src:
For $W(\Phi)=\frac{g}{3}\Phi^3,$ one obtains $\begin{gathered}
W'(\phi)=g\phi^2,
\qquad V=|g|^2|\phi|^4,\\
\mathcal L_{\mathrm{Yukawa}}
=-g\phi\psi\psi+\mathrm{h.c.}
\end{gathered}$ The quartic scalar vertex describes two-scalar scattering, while the Yukawa term is its supersymmetric companion.

